<title>USA: Disney says Pfeifer leaves record label.</title>
<headline>Disney says Pfeifer leaves record label.</headline>
<dateline>BURBANK, Calif 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Walt Disney Co said Bob Pfeifer resigned as president of its Hollywood Records unit to pursue the creative side of the music business.</p>
<p>On an interim basis, Richard Leher, executive vice president of Hollywood Records, will assume Pfeifer's duties.</p>
<p>Pfeifer joined Hollywood Records in 1993 as vice president of artists and repertoire for the label, which has been struggling becaue of a lack of hits and management turnover. He was named president in March 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;I started as a musician, and it's time for me to get back to more creative, and less administrative, pursuits,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
